I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it cannot write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or call the metadata service. Adding either would need new grants in the graph, which is a decision for whoever owns the graph definition. I also assumed the subscription URLs live under the key `"urls"`, one per line, and that a missing key means an empty list. Adjust those if the store uses a different layout.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

